1
00:00:01,502 --> 00:00:02,711
Well, if we learned

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:04,630
one thing today, Cheese,
it's that cheerleaders

3
00:00:04,672 --> 00:00:09,134
and high explosives don't mix.

4
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:11,303
Cheese:
You can say that again, Mac.

5
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,555
Well, I couldn't have done it
without you, buddy.

6
00:00:13,597 --> 00:00:14,598
You're a genius.

7
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:16,517
Oh, yeah? Well, then how come

8
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:19,353
I can't get my VCR
to stop blinking 12:00?

9
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,146
( laughter )

10
00:00:25,359 --> 00:00:27,778
So, what'd you guys think?

11
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:32,115
( phone rings )

12
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,701
I got it, I got it!
The phone, the phone!

13
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,411
Hello.

14
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:38,372
Hold on, please--
Joey, it's your mom.

15
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:39,832
It's your mommy.
Oh, that's nice.

16
00:00:39,874 --> 00:00:42,001
Ma, so what did you think?

17
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:43,752
Well

18
00:00:43,794 --> 00:00:45,754
that was, um

19
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:46,964
okay.

20
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,549
It wasn't the best.

21
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:51,927
That was one of
the worst things ever.

22
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:54,680
And not just on TV.

23
00:00:54,722 --> 00:00:56,390
What are we going
to tell him?

24
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,975
Well, the-the
lighting was okay.

25
00:00:58,017 --> 00:01:00,101
Oh, no, you don't--
you got lighting last time.

26
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,269
Lighting is mine.

27
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,688
I have costumes.

28
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:03,689
Oh, great.

29
00:01:03,731 --> 00:01:04,982
That means I'm stuck with

30
00:01:05,024 --> 00:01:07,651
"So, we were watching
you in there

31
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:10,696
and you were sitting
right here. Whoa."

32
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:12,280
What are you
going to do, Pheebs?

33
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:13,532
I don't know, I don't know.

34
00:01:13,574 --> 00:01:15,200
I can't lie to him again.

35
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:16,744
Oh, no, I'm--

36
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:19,496
No, I'm just going to press my
breasts up against him.

37
00:01:19,538 --> 00:01:21,832
And say nothing?

38
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:23,124
Uh-huh. Yeah, that's right.

39
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:25,126
All right, bye.

40
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,212
Wow, well, my folks
really liked it.

41
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:28,964
So, what did you guys think?

42
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:37,096
Well, it wasn't that good.

43
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:50,360
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

44
00:01:50,402 --> 00:01:51,653
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

45
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:54,782
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

46
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:59,494
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

47
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,705
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

48
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:05,125
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

49
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:08,462
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

50
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:11,966
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

51
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:21,600
Phoebe, do you think
that your favorite animal

52
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:23,102
says very much about you?

53
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:25,144
What, you mean
behind my back?

54
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,857
Oh! You guys, oh, my God,
you're never going to believe

55
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:30,025
what happened
to me today.

56
00:02:30,067 --> 00:02:31,735
I am sitting in my office...

57
00:02:31,777 --> 00:02:33,278
You guys, you guys,
you're not going

58
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,947
to believe what
my agent just told me.

59
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:36,239
Joey, in the middle
of a story, here.

60
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:37,825
Oh, sorry, sorry, you finish.

61
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:39,785
Okay, so anyway,
I'm sitting in my office

62
00:02:39,827 --> 00:02:40,911
and guess who walks in?

63
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:43,204
I'm going to be
on two TV shows!

64
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,456
Oh, that's great!
Really?

65
00:02:44,498 --> 00:02:46,374
Joey.

66
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:47,960
You weren't finished?
Yeah

67
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:50,378
"Guess who walks into my office"
is the end of my story.

68
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:53,132
It was Ralph Lauren.

69
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,508
Ralph Lauren
walked into my office.

70
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:55,801
Uh, Rach.

71
00:02:55,843 --> 00:02:56,885
If you're going to start
another story, at least

72
00:02:56,927 --> 00:03:00,764
let me finish mine.
It's the same story.

73
00:03:00,806 --> 00:03:03,725
Well, it's really long.

74
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:06,561
Oh, my God.
Anyway, Ralph just came in

75
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:08,271
to tell me that he's
so happy with my work

76
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:09,481
that he wants me to be

77
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,650
the new merchandising
manager for Polo retail.

78
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:14,319
Ooh.
Still get a discount
on wedding dresses?

79
00:03:14,361 --> 00:03:15,112
Yeah.

80
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:16,195
I'm so happy for you!

81
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,032
I'm so glad.

82
00:03:18,073 --> 00:03:20,951
Well, these really are
"the days of our lives."

83
00:03:20,993 --> 00:03:22,911
What?

84
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:24,371
Well, since you ask...

85
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:26,373
they want me back on
Days of our Lives.

86
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:27,415
Oh, my God.

87
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,792
I get... I get
a big pay raise!

88
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:30,335
Oh, great!

89
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:32,880
I'll be playing Drake Ramoray's
twin brother, Stryker.

90
00:03:32,921 --> 00:03:34,381
Oooh.

91
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,257
I get to hire my own assistant.

92
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,425
( squeals )

93
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,927
Well...

94
00:03:38,969 --> 00:03:41,429
I got a head rush
from standing up too fast.

95
00:03:47,186 --> 00:03:49,270
And you were at this job
for four years?

96
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,981
That's right.
Okay.

97
00:03:51,023 --> 00:03:53,232
Well, this is all
very impressive, Hilda.

98
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:56,778
Um, I just have
one last question for you.

99
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:58,279
How did I do?

100
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,531
Was this okay?

101
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:01,449
What?

102
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:03,118
I've never
interviewed anyone before.

103
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,286
I've actually never had anyone
work for me before.

104
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:07,122
Although when I was a kid
we did have a maid

105
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:08,957
but this isn't the same thing.

106
00:04:08,999 --> 00:04:11,376
No, dear. It's not.

107
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:12,502
No. Yeah.

108
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:14,880
And I know that.

109
00:04:14,922 --> 00:04:17,340
All right, well,
thank you so much for coming in.

110
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,592
It was nice to meet you.

111
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:19,718
Good meeting you.

112
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,053
All right.

113
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:24,431
I'm a total pro.

114
00:04:24,472 --> 00:04:26,183
Hello?

115
00:04:26,225 --> 00:04:27,267
Wow.

116
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:28,435
Um.

117
00:04:30,145 --> 00:04:31,312
Hi, yes, I'm sorry

118
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:32,606
the models are actually
down the hall.

119
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:35,067
Actually, I'm here
about the assistant job.

120
00:04:35,109 --> 00:04:36,068
Really?

121
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:38,112
Okay. Well, then...

122
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:39,320
All right

123
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:40,614
well, just have
a seat there.

124
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:41,782
Um, so, what's...
what is...

125
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:42,783
what's your name?

126
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,159
Tag Jones.

127
00:04:44,201 --> 00:04:46,161
Uh-huh. Go on.

128
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:48,122
That's it.

129
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:49,372
That's my whole name.

130
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:50,874
That's your whole name.

131
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:52,375
Okay, of course it is.

132
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:55,336
Okay, well, let's just
have a look-see here.

133
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:56,922
I know I haven't worked
in an office before

134
00:04:56,964 --> 00:04:58,590
and I really don't have
a lot of experience.

135
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,592
Oh, come on, now,
what are you talking about?

136
00:05:00,634 --> 00:05:03,595
You've got three years
painting houses.

137
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:07,099
Two whole summers
at T.G.I. Friday's.

138
00:05:07,141 --> 00:05:09,017
It's lame, I know.

139
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:12,104
But I'm a goal-oriented person,
very eager to learn.

140
00:05:12,146 --> 00:05:13,521
Okay, just hold on
a second, please.

141
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:19,486
Sorry, it's for Human Resources.

142
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:20,487
Everybody has to do it.

143
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,905
Would you just stand up, please?

144
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:32,582
No, no, no, no, no.

145
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:43,844
Hey.

146
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:44,678
Ch-ch-ch-ch!

147
00:05:49,141 --> 00:05:51,143
Anyway, I should go.

148
00:05:51,185 --> 00:05:52,144
Okay. Bye.

149
00:05:52,186 --> 00:05:53,436
Hey, sweetie.

150
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:54,604
Hi, sweetie.

151
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,397
So what was with
all the whispering?

152
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,732
I can't tell you.

153
00:05:57,774 --> 00:05:58,900
It's a secret.

154
00:05:58,942 --> 00:05:59,901
Secret?

155
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:01,236
Married people aren't

156
00:06:01,278 --> 00:06:03,197
supposed to have secrets
between one another.

157
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:05,782
We have too much love
and respect for one another.

158
00:06:05,824 --> 00:06:07,534
Aww.

159
00:06:07,575 --> 00:06:08,827
But still, no.

160
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:10,245
No, I'm serious.

161
00:06:10,287 --> 00:06:11,997
We should tell
each other everything.

162
00:06:12,039 --> 00:06:13,665
I do not have any
secrets from you.

163
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:14,708
Really?

164
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,293
Okay, so why don't you tell me

165
00:06:16,335 --> 00:06:18,586
what happened to Ross
junior year at Disneyland?

166
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:20,630
Oh, no, no. I can't do that.

167
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:21,882
If you tell me

168
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,258
I'll tell you
what Phoebe said.

169
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,425
Okay.

170
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:26,094
Okay.

171
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:27,721
So, Ross and I are
going to Disneyland

172
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:30,265
and we stop at this
restaurant for tacos.

173
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:33,101
And when I say restaurant,
I mean a guy, a hibachi

174
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:34,936
and the trunk of his car.

175
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:37,689
So Ross has about ten tacos

176
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:39,649
and anyway, we're on
Space Mountain

177
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:42,443
and Ross starts to feel
a little... iffy.

178
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,321
Oh, my God,
he threw up?

179
00:06:44,363 --> 00:06:47,448
No, he visited a town
a little south of throw up.

180
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:50,618
( laughing )

181
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,495
So, what was Phoebe's secret?

182
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,915
Nancy Thompson, from
Phoebe's old massage place

183
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:55,957
is getting fired.

184
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:57,500
Oh.

185
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:01,755
That's it?

186
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,798
I gave up my
Disneyland story for that?

187
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,841
That's right.

188
00:07:04,883 --> 00:07:05,967
You lose, sucker.

189
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,930
Please still marry me.

190
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,811
Chandler, you have
an assistant, right?

191
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:18,146
Did she call?

192
00:07:18,188 --> 00:07:20,315
You-you told her
I was sick, right?

193
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:22,150
Always tell her I am sick.

194
00:07:22,192 --> 00:07:23,818
No, I just don't know...

195
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,486
how do you decide who to hire?

196
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:27,864
I mean, I've got it
narrowed down to two people

197
00:07:27,906 --> 00:07:30,992
One of them has great references
and a lot of experience

198
00:07:31,034 --> 00:07:32,577
and then there's this guy...

199
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:33,578
What about him?

200
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,497
I love him.

201
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,084
He's so pretty

202
00:07:39,126 --> 00:07:40,377
I want to cry.

203
00:07:40,419 --> 00:07:41,378
I don't know what to do.

204
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:42,379
Tell me what to do.

205
00:07:42,421 --> 00:07:43,671
Come on,
you know what to do.

206
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:45,257
You hire the first one.

207
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:48,467
You don't hire an assistant
because they're cute

208
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:50,637
you hire them
because they're qualified.

209
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:53,932
Uh-huh.

210
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:57,018
No, I hear what you're saying,
and that makes a lot of sense

211
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:58,645
but can I just
say one more thing?

212
00:07:58,686 --> 00:07:59,854
Look how pretty.

213
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:02,983
Let me see.

214
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:05,652
Oh, my God.

215
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,321
Oh...

216
00:08:07,362 --> 00:08:08,905
But no.

217
00:08:08,947 --> 00:08:12,033
No, you can't hire him
'cause it's not professional.

218
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:15,245
Um, this is for me, yes?

219
00:08:15,287 --> 00:08:17,414
Okay, you're right.

220
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:19,540
I'll hire Hilda tomorrow.

221
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:22,752
Dumb old
perfect-for-the-job Hilda.

222
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,587
Let me see this guy.

223
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:28,091
Wow.

224
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,760
Don't show this to Monica.

225
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:33,430
And don't tell her
about the "wow."

226
00:08:38,435 --> 00:08:40,520
( knocking )

227
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:42,356
Hey, Joey.
Hey, Terry.

228
00:08:42,397 --> 00:08:43,398
Nice to see you again.

229
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,565
It's been awhile, huh?

230
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:45,859
Boy, it's funny.

231
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,610
These halls look smaller
than they used to.

232
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:50,238
It's a different building.

233
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:52,615
So...

234
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:54,451
Stryker Ramoray, huh?

235
00:08:54,493 --> 00:08:56,077
When do you want me to start?

236
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,246
Why don't we
start right now?

237
00:08:58,288 --> 00:08:59,539
Okay.

238
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,416
Here are the audition scenes.

239
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:06,505
Audition?

240
00:09:06,545 --> 00:09:08,298
I thought you were going
to offer me the part.

241
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:10,008
Why would you think that?

242
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:12,927
Well, I was Dr. Drake Ramoray,
Stryker's twin brother.

243
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:16,097
Who looks more like me
than me, right?

244
00:09:16,139 --> 00:09:19,434
Everybody has to audition.

245
00:09:19,476 --> 00:09:21,478
You know, Terry

246
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,105
I don't really need to do this.

247
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:26,233
I got my own cable TV series.

248
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:29,610
With a robot.

249
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:33,490
I'm sorry, Joey,
that's the way it is.

250
00:09:33,532 --> 00:09:35,492
Well...

251
00:09:35,534 --> 00:09:38,661
I guess you think
you're pretty special, huh?

252
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:42,541
Sitting up here in your
fancy small-hall building.

253
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,920
Making stars jump through
hoops for you, huh?

254
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:49,339
Well, you know what?

255
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:52,633
This is one star whose hoop...

256
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:55,762
this is a star that the hoop...
this hoop

257
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,680
I was
Dr. Drake Ramoray!

258
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:06,356
Hi, Tag.

259
00:10:06,398 --> 00:10:07,941
What are you doing here?

260
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,526
I just wanted to come by

261
00:10:09,568 --> 00:10:11,445
and thank you for not laughing
in my face yesterday.

262
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:13,654
And I noticed there aren't
any plants in your office

263
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:15,240
so I wanted
to bring you your first.

264
00:10:15,282 --> 00:10:17,992
There is a plant
in your office.

265
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,994
Kinda.

266
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,662
Right.

267
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:25,041
So, I guess I shouldn't put
"good at noticing stuff"

268
00:10:25,083 --> 00:10:26,334
on my resume.

269
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:29,003
Thank you.

270
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:31,256
Anyway, I'm guessing
you hired somebody.

271
00:10:31,298 --> 00:10:33,174
Well...

272
00:10:33,216 --> 00:10:34,426
Gotcha.

273
00:10:34,468 --> 00:10:37,471
Thanks again
for meeting with me.

274
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:40,432
But I hired you.

275
00:10:40,474 --> 00:10:42,892
What?

276
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:44,227
Yeah, you got the job.

277
00:10:44,269 --> 00:10:45,728
You're my new assistant.

278
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:46,646
I am?

279
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:47,564
Yeah.

280
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:50,442
I can't believe it.

281
00:10:50,484 --> 00:10:52,402
Me either.

282
00:10:52,444 --> 00:10:53,903
Um...

283
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:55,822
All right, first thing
I need you to do

284
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:58,074
is go downstairs and
find a woman named Hilda

285
00:10:58,116 --> 00:10:59,576
and tell her to go home.

286
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:05,123
Hey.

287
00:11:05,165 --> 00:11:06,541
Hey, good. You're home.

288
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:08,668
Oh, that's always nicer
to hear than

289
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:10,044
"Aw, crap, you again."

290
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:11,754
Hey, sweetie. Mmm...

291
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:12,755
Hey.

292
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:14,174
I made you
a surprise.

293
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:15,175
Oh, yeah?

294
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:16,510
Yeah. Tacos!

295
00:11:16,551 --> 00:11:18,261
Ever since you told me
that story

296
00:11:18,303 --> 00:11:20,679
I've had such a
craving for them.

297
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:23,391
Did you not understand
the story?

298
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:26,019
Hey.

299
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,437
Ross!
Hey, what's up?

300
00:11:27,479 --> 00:11:29,230
Nothing much.
Just trying to figure out

301
00:11:29,272 --> 00:11:30,898
what I'm going to do for dinner.

302
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,066
Huh.
You know?

303
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:33,360
Hey, whoo,
what's...

304
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,529
What's that, uh, dinner stuff?

305
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:36,863
Y-you making dinner?

306
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:38,198
( timer dings )
No. Shh!

307
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,495
What you got over there, tacos?

308
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:45,163
No. No.

309
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:47,706
They, um...
they're just, uh...

310
00:11:47,748 --> 00:11:50,877
They're... they're
ground beef smilies.

311
00:11:50,918 --> 00:11:53,712
Uh... those are tacos.

312
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:56,508
Excuse me, Mr. Mexico!

313
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,510
Uh, either way, I'll pass.

314
00:11:58,552 --> 00:12:00,220
Still can't eat those.

315
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:02,180
( wry chuckle )

316
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:05,225
( Monica stifling laughter )

317
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:08,395
( laughing )

318
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:10,146
What's so funny?

319
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:17,612
I'm not laughing.

320
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:28,081
You told her!

321
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:30,625
Nancy Thompson's getting fired.

322
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,380
Okay, okay.

323
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,797
I had food poisoning.

324
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:38,383
It's not like
I chose to do it.

325
00:12:38,425 --> 00:12:40,093
It's not like...
it's not like

326
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:42,929
I said, "Oh, what would
make this ride more fun?"

327
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:45,724
You're right. You're right.
I'm sorry.

328
00:12:45,764 --> 00:12:47,517
I shouldn't be laughing.

329
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:50,395
I should be
laying down papers for you.

330
00:12:50,437 --> 00:12:51,688
( stifling laughter )

331
00:12:51,730 --> 00:12:53,106
( laughing derisively )

332
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:54,649
How could you tell her?

333
00:12:54,691 --> 00:12:56,484
I had to, okay?
We're getting married.

334
00:12:56,526 --> 00:12:59,070
Married couples can't keep
secrets from one another.

335
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:00,614
Oh, really? Well, I...

336
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,198
I guess Monica should know
about Atlantic City.

337
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,033
Du-ude!

338
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:06,035
What happened
in Atlantic City?

339
00:13:06,077 --> 00:13:08,037
Well, Chandler and I
were in a bar...

340
00:13:08,079 --> 00:13:10,624
Did you not hear me say,
"Du-ude!"?

341
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:13,876
And this girl is making
eyes at Chandler. Okay?

342
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:16,504
So, after a while, he...
he goes over to her

343
00:13:16,546 --> 00:13:19,798
and, uh... after a minute
or two, I see them kissing.

344
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,426
Now, I know what
you're thinking.

345
00:13:21,468 --> 00:13:23,637
Chandler's not type of guy
who just goes to bars

346
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:25,054
and makes out with girls.

347
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:27,181
And you're right, Chandler's
not the type of guy

348
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:31,810
who just goes to bars
and makes out with girls.

349
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:34,855
You kissed a guy?! Oh!

350
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,776
Oh, my God!

351
00:13:37,816 --> 00:13:42,614
In my defense, it was dark,
and he was a very pretty guy.

352
00:13:42,656 --> 00:13:44,073
( laughing harder )

353
00:13:44,115 --> 00:13:46,242
Oh, Mon,
I laughed so hard.

354
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:50,622
Ho-ho! So hard we had to throw
out your underwear again?

355
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:54,668
Whatever, dude,
you kissed a guy.

356
00:14:00,173 --> 00:14:01,924
Hi.
Hey.
Hey.

357
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,884
Ooh, how's Hilda?
She working out?

358
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:08,515
Oh, my new assistant is...
working out, yes.

359
00:14:09,516 --> 00:14:11,309
Was she happy
you gave her the job?

360
00:14:11,351 --> 00:14:13,770
Oh, my-my new assistant
was very happy

361
00:14:13,812 --> 00:14:15,814
that I hired my new assistant.

362
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:17,023
( phone ringing )

363
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:19,858
Hello.

364
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,068
Oh, hey.

365
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,237
Can you, uh, can you
hang on a second?

366
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:25,532
It's the producers
over at Mac and Cheese.

367
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,367
If you'll excuse me
for a minute.

368
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:30,704
Hey, funny
you should call.

369
00:14:30,745 --> 00:14:33,247
I was just looking over
next week's script.

370
00:14:34,541 --> 00:14:36,292
Canceled?!

371
00:14:36,334 --> 00:14:38,837
Like they're taking it
off the air?

372
00:14:38,877 --> 00:14:40,672
Joey:
Oh.

373
00:14:40,714 --> 00:14:41,715
All right.

374
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:43,508
I'll see you Monday.

375
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:46,761
We're not even shooting
them anymore?!

376
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:48,346
Well, all right.

377
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,472
Bye.

378
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:53,059
They canceled
Mac and Cheese!

379
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,019
I'm sorry.
Oh, Joey,
sorry, Joey.

380
00:14:55,061 --> 00:14:56,354
Why would they do that?

381
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:58,022
That was a good show, right?

382
00:15:09,534 --> 00:15:11,661
You want to tell secrets?
Okay, okay.

383
00:15:11,703 --> 00:15:15,122
In college,
Ross used to wear leg warmers.

384
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:16,791
( laughs )

385
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:18,585
All right. All right.

386
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:22,505
Chandler entered a Vanilla Ice
look-alike contest and won.

387
00:15:22,547 --> 00:15:26,509
Ross came in fourth and cried!

388
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:28,469
( laughing ):
Oh, my God!

389
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:29,512
Oh, is that funny?

390
00:15:29,554 --> 00:15:31,222
Oh, you-you find that funny?

391
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:34,726
Well, maybe Chandler should know
some of your secrets, too.

392
00:15:34,768 --> 00:15:37,562
( laughing ):
I... I already told him
everything.

393
00:15:37,604 --> 00:15:39,146
You shush!

394
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:42,191
Once, Monica was sent
to her room without dinner

395
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:45,528
so she ate the macaroni
off a jewelry box she'd made.

396
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:46,863
Aah!

397
00:15:46,905 --> 00:15:48,239
Um...

398
00:15:48,281 --> 00:15:50,700
Ross used to stay home
every Saturday night

399
00:15:50,742 --> 00:15:52,034
to watch Golden Girls.

400
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:57,123
Monica couldn't tell time
until she was 13.

401
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,544
It's hard for some people.

402
00:16:01,586 --> 00:16:03,922
Of course it is.

403
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:08,301
Chandler one time wore
my underwear to work!

404
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:09,886
Hey!

405
00:16:09,928 --> 00:16:13,222
I'm sorry I couldn't think
of any more for Ross.

406
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:14,557
Ross:
Oh, oh!

407
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:16,225
In college, Chandler got drunk

408
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,728
and slept with the lady
who cleaned our dorm.

409
00:16:18,770 --> 00:16:19,978
( laughs )

410
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:22,064
That was you.

411
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:24,317
( Monica laughs )

412
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:26,736
Whatever, dude,
you kissed a guy.

413
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:31,532
How could this happen to me?

414
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:34,285
Yesterday I had two TV shows.

415
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:36,496
Today I've got nothing.

416
00:16:36,537 --> 00:16:37,872
Well, wait a minute.

417
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:39,582
What happened
to Days of Our Lives?

418
00:16:39,624 --> 00:16:42,919
Uh, well, they might be
a little mad at me over there.

419
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:44,629
Wh-wh-what happened?

420
00:16:44,671 --> 00:16:46,965
Well, maybe I got
a little upset

421
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:50,176
and maybe I told them
where they could go.

422
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:52,720
Joey, why would you do that?

423
00:16:52,762 --> 00:16:55,431
Because they wanted me
to audition.

424
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:57,266
You?! An actor?!

425
00:16:57,308 --> 00:16:59,059
That's madness!

426
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,902
Rachel Green's office.

427
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:11,948
Tag?

428
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:13,574
Hi. Who was that?

429
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:14,951
Nobody.

430
00:17:14,993 --> 00:17:17,077
I was just practicing.

431
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,412
Really?

432
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:21,040
( tittering )

433
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,043
Hi.

434
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:26,921
Hi. Rachel
Green's office.

435
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:30,842
You must be Hilda.

436
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:33,135
Yeah, this is Tag.

437
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:34,345
Tag, this is Phoebe.

438
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:36,180
Phoebe, could I see you
for a second?

439
00:17:36,222 --> 00:17:37,515
Phoebe...
Mm-hmm.

440
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:38,850
That's a great name.

441
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:39,851
Oh, you like that?

442
00:17:39,893 --> 00:17:41,394
You should hear my phone number.

443
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,437
Okay. We'll
be right back.

444
00:17:45,023 --> 00:17:47,859
Mmm...

445
00:17:47,901 --> 00:17:51,278
So, you hired yourself
a little treat, did ya?

446
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,072
All right, I know.

447
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:54,866
I know how it
looks, Pheebs, but
I'm telling you...

448
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:57,451
But-but you know you cannot get
involved with your assistant.

449
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:58,995
Yes, I know that.
I know that.

450
00:17:59,037 --> 00:18:00,747
And I know
that hiring him

451
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:02,790
was probably not the smartest
thing that I've ever done

452
00:18:02,832 --> 00:18:04,542
but I'm telling you,
from this moment on

453
00:18:04,584 --> 00:18:06,210
I swear,
this is strictly professional.

454
00:18:06,252 --> 00:18:07,294
( knock on door )
Yes?

455
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:08,713
Rachel:
Hi.
Hey Rachel.

456
00:18:08,755 --> 00:18:10,048
Cute assistant.

457
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,632
What's his story?

458
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:12,800
Is he...?

459
00:18:12,842 --> 00:18:14,552
Gay? Yeah.

460
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:18,598
( knock on door )

461
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:20,182
Hey...

462
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:22,101
Terry.

463
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:24,102
Joey Tribbiani!

464
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:28,024
Surprised your big head could
fit through our small halls.

465
00:18:28,066 --> 00:18:29,525
I got to go, Joey.

466
00:18:29,567 --> 00:18:31,527
Wait, Terry,
look, wait, uh...

467
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:33,571
I'm really sorry
about before.

468
00:18:33,613 --> 00:18:36,532
I was an idiot, thinking I'm
too big to audition for you.

469
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:38,284
You got to give me
another chance.

470
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:39,452
I can't help
you, Joey.

471
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:41,495
Wait, Terry, please!

472
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:43,121
Look...

473
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:45,499
I just lost my other job, okay?

474
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:48,335
You have no idea
how much I need this.

475
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:49,963
Please, help me out.

476
00:18:50,004 --> 00:18:53,340
For old times' sake.

477
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:55,551
This poor guy's
been in a coma
for five years.

478
00:18:55,593 --> 00:18:56,552
It's hopeless.

479
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:57,971
It's not hopeless.

480
00:18:58,012 --> 00:19:00,139
Dr. Stryker Ramoray's
a miracle worker.

481
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,432
Look, here he comes.

482
00:19:01,474 --> 00:19:03,309
Good morning.

483
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:12,693
Drake, it's your
brother, Stryker.

484
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:14,487
Can you hear me?

485
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:16,530
Director:
And... cut!

486
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:21,452
I'm back, baby! Ha, ha, ha!

487
00:19:32,797 --> 00:19:35,758
You know, in my defense, um...

488
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:39,595
there was no glitter on the
macaroni and very little glue.

489
00:19:39,637 --> 00:19:43,599
And in my defense,
the cleaning lady came on to me.

490
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:46,560
You have no trouble
telling time now, right?

491
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,561
No.

492
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,022
Quick,
what time is it?

493
00:19:49,063 --> 00:19:51,065
I don't know.
Time to kiss a guy, maybe?

494
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:54,193
( chuckling )

495
00:19:54,234 --> 00:19:56,863
What are you laughing at,
Pampers?

496
00:19:58,948 --> 00:20:02,160
You know, when I said that
because we're getting married

497
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:05,204
we should share everything
and not have any secrets?

498
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:06,205
Yeah.

499
00:20:06,246 --> 00:20:07,498
Yeah, that was stupid.

500
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:08,582
Let's not do that.

501
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:11,210
Oh. Absolutely.

502
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:14,380
And we should keep all the stuff
we told each other secret

503
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:15,548
from everybody else.

504
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:17,299
Yeah, definitely.

505
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:18,801
( chuckling )

506
00:20:18,843 --> 00:20:21,054
Okay, if you'll excuse me

507
00:20:21,095 --> 00:20:22,763
I'm going to go hang out

508
00:20:22,805 --> 00:20:25,432
with some people who don't know
the Space Mountain story.

509
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:28,061
Then I'd steer
clear of Phoebe.

510
00:20:28,102 --> 00:20:29,896
Man!

511
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:30,980
Well.

512
00:20:31,022 --> 00:20:32,606
Yeah, not that you would

513
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:35,860
but I wouldn't go hang out
with all the guys at my office.

514
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:45,786
( knock at door )

515
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,580
Hi.

516
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:50,833
Do you have a minute?

517
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:52,459
Oh, yeah, sure. What's up?

518
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:56,547
I got asked out twice today
while I was at lunch...

519
00:20:56,589 --> 00:20:58,549
by guys.

520
00:20:58,591 --> 00:21:00,760
Really?

521
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:02,095
Yeah.

522
00:21:02,136 --> 00:21:04,638
Did you tell someone
that I was gay?

523
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:08,226
Oh, did you not want people
to know that?

524
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:10,686
No, I'm not gay.

525
00:21:10,728 --> 00:21:14,314
And I especially wouldn't
want you to think I was gay.

526
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:16,859
Why's that?

527
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:19,612
I don't think I should say.

528
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:21,781
Oh, you can say.

529
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,365
Come on.

530
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:27,285
I don't want you to feel like
you can't tell me things.

531
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:30,123
Okay.

532
00:21:30,164 --> 00:21:31,124
'kay.

533
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:32,708
Well?

534
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,127
Yeah.

535
00:21:34,168 --> 00:21:36,754
I'd love to ask out
